{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/809909-clarity-and-you","id":809909,"title":"Clarity and You","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-15T16:26:04-08:00","id":809909,"title":"Clarity and You","content":"I'm still new to the game, and thought I'd collect some opinions from experienced players and storytellers on how to handle Clarity, both mechanically and in terms of role playing.<ul><li>How much does a PC's Clarity typically vary over a chronicle?</li> <li>Do PCs tend to settle around a particular range, is it a roller coaster ride, or a struggle to prevent the decline into madness?</li> <li>How do you depict low Clarity NPCs?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T07:00:37-08:00","id":810210,"title":"","content":"Q1. Depends on the Changeling and the events unfolding<br /> Q2. see answer 1.<br /> Q3. Delusional, they have a harder time telling the difference between mortal world and fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:17:18-08:00","id":810233,"title":"","content":"1) Most of my games have players sticking around their starting Clarity (7, or 5 if they wanted the XP), unless they take specific effort to make it drop.<br /> 2) Once they start dropping, however, it tends to be like a rock; a few have managed to scrape back up, but most don't think it's worth the XP.<br /> 3) Starting at Clarity 4, characters start having halucinations. Some are blatent (bleeding walls, little blue men), some are subtle (smell of metal, sounds of animals in the walls, someone calling for help distantly). Additionally, characters suffer from the Condition Halucinations (which was modified from Madness): The GM has a pool of dice equal to 10 \u2013 (character\u2019s Clarity). Once per game, the GM can apply those dice as a negative modifier to any Mental or Social roll made for the character due to them seeing something that others cannot perceive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}